// SUPERSEDED 2026-08-29 (the bottom-ride deletion): the ride this
// fixture pinned is gone. A bottom scrutinee now BOTTOMS the select on
// both engines (no held-arm ride), so this program agrees by bottoming
// out. The historical description below documents the deleted behavior.
//
// aug01b reactive divergence_000000 (2026-08-02): the select MERGE is an
// interior-bottom taint ORIGIN — its producing site changes when the
// selection switches, so a newly-taken arm that bottoms (100 % 0) has no
// op-site history even though the select's value stream does (arm 1 fed
// u8:1 on the initial epoch). The node-walk's consumer Cached rides the
// stream's last value and the downstream select re-fires its selected
// arm on in0; the unwrapped merge taint instead poisoned the consuming
// dispatch — jit missed the injection-cycle fire (interp [1];[2], jit
// [1];[]). Fixed by wrapping the scalar select merge in
// emit_scalar_taint_cache like every other origin site.
// schedule-v1: cap=112 events=896; in0=i64:1
{
  let v0 = select in0 {
    i64:0 => u8:1,
    _ => u8:100 % u8:0
  };
  select v0 {
    u8:100 => i64:0,
    _ => in0 + i64:1
  }
}